cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "How far can NeuralFoil be trusted below Re = 500,000? A two-tunnel wind-tunnel benchmark with an XFoil error decomposition, and robust low-Reynolds-number airfoil design"
abstract: >-
  A two-tunnel wind-tunnel benchmark of the NeuralFoil surrogate below
  Re = 500,000: 9,100 clean drag-polar points on 94 airfoils from the UIUC
  Low-Speed Airfoil Tests archive and the Princeton "Airfoils at Low Speeds"
  data set, plus tripped runs and lift sweeps through stall. Headless XFoil is
  run at every point so the error is split into XFoil's physics error and the
  network's emulation error; a tunnel-to-tunnel comparison gives the
  experimental noise floor; NeuralFoil is run on the measured as-built model
  shapes; statistics use an airfoil-cluster bootstrap; and a cross-validated
  Gamma GLM predicts the expected drag error from confidence, Re, angle of
  attack, camber and thickness. Also a reproducible pipeline for robust,
  multi-objective, manufacturing-tolerant airfoil optimization with
  AeroSandbox, and a confidence-aware optimizer that uses the measured
  reliability inside the design loop.
